<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Maldives</h1><p class="st-meta">1968 CE – present · capital Male</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Indian Ocean island republic of the Maldives, transformed by tourism and threatened by rising sea levels.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After independence from British protection in 1965, a referendum in 1968 abolished the Sultanate of the Maldives and established a presidential republic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-nasir">Ibrahim Nasir</a>, the former prime minister, became the first president on 11 November 1968, governing the atolls from Male.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nasir developed tourism from 1972 and fishing modernisation. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maumoon-abdul-gayoom">Maumoon Abdul Gayoom</a> ruled from 1978 to 2008, surviving a coup attempt in 1988 that was defeated with Indian help, while restricting opposition. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> is the state religion. The 2004 tsunami devastated many islands, and the low-lying country has become a voice for climate action.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>A new constitution in 2008 introduced multiparty elections, won by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohamed-nasheed">Mohamed Nasheed</a>. His resignation under pressure in 2012 began a period of political turmoil, and the republic continues with competitive elections.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-maldives.jpg" alt="Republic of Maldives" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: See File history, below, for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Maldives.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1968 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Male</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ibrahim Nasir, Maumoon Abdul Gayoom, Mohamed Nasheed</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dhivehi</dd><dt>Tod